  "worked_solution": "We have that the battery duration $L(t)$ is measured in hours and the charging time is measured in minutes. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t): & \\text{hours} \\\\ t: & \\text{minutes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}$ measures a change in $L(t)$ over a change in $t.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{minute}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, $\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}$ is measured in \"hours per minute\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
